  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 104 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nA quiet pattern continues through at least Friday with highs \ngenerally in the 60s/70s and low in the 40s. Our next storm system \nis due to arrive this weekend bringing our next chance of rain. An \nupper trough will weaken over N. Mexico before reaching our area \nlate Friday into Saturday. Even so, lift will increase ahead of the \ntrough with Gulf moisture already in place to bring a good chance \n(>50%) of showers and isolated storms to the western half of the \nCWA. This area of rain will move west to east across then entire \nregion through the day Saturday. At this time, amounts look to be \ngenerally under 0.5\", except for the higher terrain where heavier \namounts could fall due to better lift. Temperatures will remain near \nto above normal with this system bringing Pacific air with it. \n\nA stronger cold front is possible Sunday into Monday as another \nstorm system moves across the Plains. Details with that front \nuncertain, but it should bring temperatures closer, if not below\nnormal.",
